    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14297" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποχετ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>draw off</i> water <i>by a canal,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				736b
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ ῥεῦμα ἀπωχετευμένον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>R.</u>
					485d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				867b13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				12.2
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πλάτων ἀπὸ τοῦ Ὁμηρικοῦ νάματος
					εἰς αὑτὸν μυρίας παρατροπὰς -σάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Longin.
					13.3
				</span></i>
			:—so in 
				Act.
			, 'canalize', 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν Ὁμήρου ποίησιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					2.51a
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τὸ βάσκανον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.485e
				</span></i>
			.</div>
